        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The U.S. military is actively developing new drone technologies, with companies vying for the development of a lower-cost drone to succeed the MQ-9 Reaper. Taiwan has received its first two F-16 Block 70 fighters, marking a significant milestone in its military capabilities. Ukraine has used its domestically developed FP-7 tactical ballistic missile in combat for the first time, enhancing its capabilities. The U.S. Army Corps of Engineers is beginning maintenance dredging at Everett Harbor and Snohomish River, expected to start in the lower settling basin as early as Oct. 16, 2026. The F-16 fleet in Ukraine is facing increasing pressure due to the demands of the air war, with shortages of air-to-air missiles now compounded by a shortage of personnel. Latvia is moving toward acquiring Anduril Industries’ Barracuda family of long-range strike missiles, enhancing its long-range strike capabilities. The U.S. military is also developing a missile warning system for its F-15EX Eagle II fighters, improving their operational capabilities.</description>
        <Point>
